# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env (git-ignored).
# Same values go to Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# WARNING: every VITE_ var ships inside the public JS bundle — never put a
# service_role key or any secret here. anon key is public by design (RLS guards it).

# Admin gate (local dev only — no Supabase below). The production bundle
# contains NO fallback password; Brand Studio then needs a signed-in account
# with profiles.role = 'admin' (see step 4).
VITE_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@huda-gymwear.co.uk
VITE_ADMIN_PASS=huda2026
# Production domain, no trailing slash. Used for canonical/OG tags + sitemap.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://hudagymwear.vercel.app
# Supabase — turns on shared catalog, orders, reviews, uploads + staff admin auth.
# The storefront is guest-only: no shopper signup/login. Brand Studio staff
# sign in with Supabase Auth accounts that carry profiles.role = 'admin'.
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com, copy URL + anon key here.
# 2. SQL editor → run, IN ORDER:
#      supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql      (tables, RLS, triggers)
#      supabase/migrations/0002_storage.sql    (product-images bucket)
#      supabase/migrations/0003_security.sql   (hardened RLS — REQUIRED)
#      supabase/migrations/0004_production.sql (catalog/settings/discounts/
#        inbox tables, server-side pricing trigger, guest lookup, receipts)
#      supabase/migrations/0005_fix.sql        (anon grant for is_admin so
#        guest checkout works + RPC surface hardening — REQUIRED)
#      supabase/migrations/0006_realtime_and_categories.sql
#      supabase/migrations/0007_open_reviews.sql (guest review inserts)
#      supabase/migrations/0008_remove_shopper_accounts.sql (drops addresses,
#        guest-order claiming, shopper self-service policies — REQUIRED)
#      supabase/migrations/0009_push_subscriptions.sql (admin devices that want
#        alerts with the app closed — only needed for Web Push, see below)
# 3. Authentication → Sign In / Sign Up: enable Email (used for STAFF sign-in
#    only). Google provider: DISABLE (shopper Google login is removed).
#    Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration:
#      Site URL = your production domain (e.g. https://huda-gymwear.vercel.app)
#      No storefront redirect URLs are needed anymore (no /account pages).
#      Keep http://localhost:8080 for local dev if you test auth locally.
# 4. First admin (shopper self-provisioning is removed, so do it in SQL):
#    a. Dashboard → Authentication → Users → Add user (create staff login).
#    b. Copy the new user's UUID, then SQL editor →
#      insert into public.profiles (id, email, name, role)
#      values ('<paste-uuid>', 'staff@example.co.uk', 'Staff Name', 'admin');
#    Further staff: an existing admin can't create profiles from the app —
#    repeat (a)+(b), or temporarily re-add a self-insert policy.
# 5. Removing a staff auth identity fully needs the service_role key or the
#    Dashboard → Authentication → Users. Order records stay for tax law.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional: admin alerts while the app is fully closed (Web Push). Public key
# only — generate with `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys --json`, then do the
# rest of the one-time setup in supabase/PUSH_SETUP.md (migration 0009 + the
# order-push Edge Function holds the private key, never this bundle).
# Left empty, the app is completely inert: no subscription, no extra requests.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
